      "post_id": "2091281011095347566",
      "url": "https://x.com/BraveReport/status/2091281011095347566",
      "text": "The Charlie Kirk report written by VFT screenshotted by @gabbylovesusa in her thread here is one of the most laughable things I’ve ever read.\n\nTHIS is who our government is listening to?\n\nTalk about needing absolutely no evidence establishing attribution, coordination, or causation for anything they report. The TPUSA/Wilson contingent should really be demanding positive evidence for these extraordinary claims, but, of course, they won’t.\n\nOne example VFT apparently finds suspicious is a tiny account that has posted Temu coupons alongside their political replies 😂😂 Whenever I go onto the SHEIN app, I’m bombarded with popups encouraging me to share coupons to my X account. Posting referral spam for a ecommerce company that happens to be Chinese is not evidence that someone is participating in a Chinese information operation. Talk about a stretch.\n\nAndrew Tate is bizarrely included under “foreign operators,” with his legal proceedings in Romania highlighted as though that makes him a Romanian influence operation. He’s a dual U.S.-British citizen. An American posting “civil war” after an American political assassination is not evidence of foreign influence.\n\nThen they label “U.S. Homeland Security News” as a “Russian influence node, based on language and posting history.” One example they show is an ENGLISH post of theirs quoting and translating Russian from the Minneapolis SHOOTER’S NOTEBOOK. 😂 The Russian came from the shooter, not the account. If they have actual evidence connecting this account to Russia, where is it?\n\nThe entire report seems built around the same bizarre assumption that a supposed foreign actor expresses an opinion, Americans subsequently express the same opinion, and therefore the foreign actor must have “seeded” the narrative and Americans are merely repeating it.\n\nIt totally ignores that Americans have their own working eyes, ears and brains. We can observe events, make deductions and independently arrive at the same conclusions as people in other countries. An Iranian, Russian, Pakistani, Turkish, or Israeli, person saying something first does not establish that Americans who later say it got the idea FROM THEM.\n\nPlease make the madness stop.",
      "original_text": "The Charlie Kirk report written by VFT screenshotted by @gabbylovesusa in her thread here is one of the most laughable things I’ve ever read.\n\nTHIS is who our government is listening to?\n\nTalk about needing absolutely no evidence establishing attribution, coordination, or causation for anything they report. The TPUSA/Wilson contingent should really be demanding positive evidence for these extraordinary claims, but, of course, they won’t.\n\nOne example VFT apparently finds suspicious is a tiny account that has posted Temu coupons alongside their  political replies 😂😂 Whenever I go onto the SHEIN app, I’m bombarded with popups encouraging me to share coupons to my X account. Posting referral spam for a ecommerce company that happens to be Chinese is not evidence that someone is participating in a Chinese information operation. Talk about a stretch.\n\nAndrew Tate is bizarrely included under “foreign operators,” with his legal proceedings in Romania highlighted as though that makes him a Romanian influence operation. He’s a dual U.S.-British citizen. An American posting “civil war” after an American political assassination is not evidence of foreign influence.\n\nThen they label “U.S. Homeland Security News” as a “Russian influence node, based on language and posting history.” One example they show is an ENGLISH post of theirs quoting and translating Russian from the Minneapolis SHOOTER’S NOTEBOOK. 😂 The Russian came from the shooter, not the account. If they have actual evidence connecting this account to Russia, where is it?\n\nThe entire report seems built around the same bizarre assumption that a supposed foreign actor expresses an opinion, Americans subsequently express the same opinion, and therefore the foreign actor must have “seeded” the narrative and Americans are merely repeating it.\n\nIt totally ignores that Americans have their own working eyes, ears and brains. We can observe events, make deductions and independently arrive at the same conclusions as people in other countries. An Iranian, Russian, Pakistani, Turkish, or Israeli, person saying something first does not establish that Americans who later say it got the idea FROM THEM.\n\nPlease make the madness stop.",
      "links": [],
      "translation_zh": "由 VFT 撰写、@gabbylovesusa 在她这里的串帖中截图的 Charlie Kirk 报告，是我读过的最可笑的东西之一。\n\n这就是我们的政府在听取的人？\n\n他们报告任何事情时，简直完全不需要任何证据来确立归因、协调或因果关系。TPUSA/Wilson 阵营真的应该要求这些非同寻常的说法拿出正面证据，但当然，他们不会。\n\nVFT 显然觉得可疑的一个例子，是一个很小的账号，它在政治回复旁边发过 Temu 优惠券 😂😂 每当我打开 SHEIN app，就会被弹窗轰炸，鼓励我把优惠券分享到我的 X 账号。给一家碰巧是中国的电商公司发推荐垃圾信息，并不能证明某人在参与中国的信息行动。真是太牵强了。\n\nAndrew Tate 被莫名其妙地列在“外国操作者”下面，还强调了他在罗马尼亚的法律程序，好像这就让他成了罗马尼亚影响力行动的一部分。他是美国和英国双重国籍。一个美国人在一起美国政治暗杀事件后发“内战”，并不是外国影响的证据。\n\n然后他们把“U.S. Homeland Security News”标记为“俄罗斯影响力节点，依据是语言和发帖历史”。他们展示的一个例子，是该账号的一条英文帖子，引用并翻译了明尼阿波利斯枪手笔记本里的俄语。😂 俄语来自枪手，不是来自这个账号。如果他们有把这个账号同俄罗斯联系起来的实际证据，证据在哪里？\n\n整份报告似乎建立在同一个离奇的假设之上：某个所谓的外国行为者表达了一个观点，美国人随后表达了同样的观点，因此这个外国行为者一定“播种”了这种叙事，而美国人只是复述它。\n\n这完全无视了美国人有自己正常运作的眼睛、耳朵和大脑。我们可以观察事件，作出推断，并独立得出与其他国家的人相同的结论。一名伊朗、俄罗斯、巴基斯坦、土耳其或以色列人先说了什么，并不能证明后来这么说的美国人是从他们那里得到这个想法的。\n\n请让这种疯狂停下来。",
